# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query the required inputs and expected outputs {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"
msgstr "I-query ang mga kinakailangang input at inaasahang output {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The easiest way to see the required inputs and expected outputs is to print the [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") object. Array items are formatted as `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, and the required inputs precede the optional inputs.\n"
msgstr "Ang pinakamadaling paraan para makita ang mga kinakailangang input at inaasahang output ay i-print ang [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") object. Ang mga array item ay naka-format bilang `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, at nauuna ang mga kinakailangang input bago ang mga opsyonal na input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") and [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of the samplex, as well as more detailed information like their names, shapes, types, and descriptions, can also be queried programatically. The return type of both of these methods is a [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). For example, the following code lists all specifications of the input interface:\n"
msgstr "Ang [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") at [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") ng samplex, pati ang mas detalyadong impormasyon tulad ng mga pangalan, hugis, uri, at paglalarawan ng mga ito, ay maaari ring i-query nang programmatic. Ang return type ng dalawang method na ito ay isang [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). Halimbawa, inililista ng sumusunod na code ang lahat ng specification ng input interface:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next example prints some information about those output specifiers whose names contain the string `\"flips\"`.\n"
msgstr "Ipi-print ng susunod na halimbawa ang ilang impormasyon tungkol sa mga output specifier na ang mga pangalan ay naglalaman ng string na `\"flips\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input values and sample {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"
msgstr "I-bind ang mga input value at mag-sample {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), the samplex needs values for at least those [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") that are marked as required. These values are first bound to an input interface so that it can perform all necessary type checking (or type coercion in some cases) and shape analysis. If anything is wrong with the types or shapes, or if a required value is missing, a verbose error is raised.\n"
msgstr "Para ma-[`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), kailangan ng samplex ng mga value para sa hindi bababa sa mga [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") na minarkahang kinakailangan. Ang mga value na ito ay unang bina-bind sa isang input interface para maisagawa nito ang lahat ng kinakailangang type checking (o type coercion sa ilang kaso) at shape analysis. Kung may mali sa mga uri o hugis, o kung may kulang na kinakailangang value, magtataas ng verbose na error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input {#bind-input}"
msgstr "I-bind ang input {#bind-input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method is passed the required input values. It is then used to draw three randomizations from the samplex. The required bindings from the dressings are the Pauli Lindblad maps for noise injection and the basis change array. Additionally, values for the four parameters in the original boxed circuit are required, which in this case is set to `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. The samplex composes these parameters into the dressings, so they effectively become modifications to the samplex’s output parameter values.\n"
msgstr "Sa sumusunod na halimbawa, ipinapasa sa method na [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") ang mga kinakailangang input value. Ginagamit ito pagkatapos para kumuha ng tatlong randomization mula sa samplex. Ang mga kinakailangang binding mula sa mga dressing ay ang mga Pauli Lindblad map para sa noise injection at ang basis change array. Bukod dito, kailangan ang mga value para sa apat na parameter sa orihinal na boxed circuit, na sa kasong ito ay itinakda sa `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. Isinasama ng samplex ang mga parameter na ito sa mga dressing, kaya epektibo silang nagiging mga pagbabago sa mga output parameter value ng samplex.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs can be bound to the interface through multiple calls to [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") or by direct item assignment. Despite the nested dictionary format that [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") allows for convenience, it is a flat mapping object, and supports all of the usual mapping syntax. Once all required inputs have been found, [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\") becomes true.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring i-bind ang mga input sa interface sa pamamagitan ng maraming tawag sa [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") o sa direktang item assignment. Bagama't pinapayagan ng [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") ang nested dictionary format para sa kaginhawahan, isa itong flat mapping object, at sinusuportahan nito ang lahat ng karaniwang mapping syntax. Kapag nahanap na ang lahat ng kinakailangang input, magiging true ang [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") objects, including the [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\") subclass, map objects against data that has been bound to them. This means that you can get, for example, the template parameter values as follows. In this case, it has shape `(3, 48)` since three randomizations were requested and the template circuit has 48 parameters.\n"
msgstr "Lahat ng [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") object, kasama ang subclass na [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\"), ay nagma-map ng mga object laban sa data na nabind sa mga ito. Ibig sabihin, makukuha mo, halimbawa, ang mga template parameter value gaya ng sumusunod. Sa kasong ito, ang hugis nito ay `(3, 48)` dahil tatlong randomization ang hiniling at ang template circuit ay may 48 parameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify input as a dictionary {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang input bilang dictionary {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of providing a fully-bound [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), you can specify the inputs as a standard dictionary, as is shown in the cell below. In this case, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method internally binds the dictionary items to the samplex’s input interface to validate that all required inputs are present and compatible.\n"
msgstr "Sa halip na magbigay ng ganap na nabind na [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), maaari mong tukuyin ang mga input bilang karaniwang dictionary, gaya ng ipinapakita sa cell sa ibaba. Sa kasong ito, internal na bina-bind ng method na [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") ang mga item ng dictionary sa input interface ng samplex para i-validate na naroroon at compatible ang lahat ng kinakailangang input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input types {#input-types}"
msgstr "Mga uri ng input {#input-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Currently, there are two interface value types:\n"
msgstr "Sa kasalukuyan, may dalawang uri ng interface value:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Array-valued: These have a shape and a data type. Bound values are coerced into the data type if possible. Any dimension can be a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Array-valued: May hugis at data type ang mga ito. Ang mga bound na value ay kino-coerce sa data type kung posible. Anumang dimensyon ay maaaring maging free dimension.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli Lindblad maps: These must be of type [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) and must act on the prescribed number of qubits. The number of terms in the map is a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Mga Pauli Lindblad map: Dapat ay may uri na [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) at dapat umaksyon sa itinakdang bilang ng mga qubit. Ang bilang ng mga term sa map ay isang free dimension.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Free dimensions {#free-dimensions}"
msgstr "Mga free dimension {#free-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") class has a notion of *free dimensions*, which are named integer sizes whose values are undetermined until some data has been bound to the interface that constrains them. All free dimensions of the same name must resolve to a consistent size when binding data, or an error will be raised. For example, in the [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of any samplex, the array axis corresponding to randomizations is a free parameter that has the name `\"num_randomizations\"` by convention. When `sample()` is called, it binds values to the outputs\n"
msgstr "Ang class na [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") ay may konsepto ng mga *free dimension*, na mga pinangalanang integer size na ang mga value ay hindi pa tiyak hangga't walang data na nabind sa interface na naglilimita sa mga ito. Lahat ng free dimension na magkapareho ang pangalan ay dapat mag-resolve sa pare-parehong laki kapag nagbi-bind ng data, kung hindi ay magtataas ng error. Halimbawa, sa [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") ng anumang samplex, ang array axis na tumutugma sa mga randomization ay isang free parameter na may pangalang `\"num_randomizations\"` ayon sa kumbensyon. Kapag tinawag ang `sample()`, nagbi-bind ito ng mga value sa mga output\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another common free-dimension scenario is sharing term constraints between Pauli lindblad map specifications and their modifiers. A [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) is an ordered sequence of terms, where each term contains a floating point rate and a sparse Pauli representation. The [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function adds a specifier `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` for this type for each [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation, and if it contains a `modifier_ref`, a `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"` specifier is also added. Both of these share the free dimension `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` that specifies how many Pauli Lindblad terms are present in the noise model because the latter needs to zip against the rates of the former to scale them.\n"
msgstr "Isa pang karaniwang free-dimension na sitwasyon ay ang pagbabahagi ng mga term constraint sa pagitan ng mga specification ng Pauli lindblad map at ng mga modifier ng mga ito. Ang [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) ay isang ordered na sequence ng mga term, kung saan bawat term ay may floating point na rate at sparse na Pauli representation. Nagdaragdag ang function na [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") ng specifier na `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` para sa uring ito para sa bawat [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation, at kung may `modifier_ref` ito, may idinaragdag ding specifier na `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"`. Parehong ibinabahagi ng dalawang ito ang free dimension na `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` na tumutukoy kung ilang Pauli Lindblad term ang nasa noise model dahil kailangang i-zip ng huli laban sa mga rate ng una para i-scale ang mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qubit-ordering-convention\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit ordering convention {#qubit-ordering-convention}"
msgstr "Kumbensyon sa pagkakasunod ng mga qubit {#qubit-ordering-convention}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplexes constructed from boxed circuits by the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function can require array-valued inputs to [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), where one index corresponds to qubits in a circuit’s box. This section explains the ordering convention that should be used for such axes. In summary: use the qubit order of the boxed circuit, restricted to the box’s qubits.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga samplex na binuo mula sa mga boxed circuit gamit ang function na [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") ay maaaring mangailangan ng array-valued na mga input sa [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), kung saan ang isang index ay tumutugma sa mga qubit sa box ng circuit. Ipinapaliwanag ng seksyong ito ang kumbensyon sa pagkakasunod na dapat gamitin para sa mga ganoong axis. Sa madaling sabi: gamitin ang pagkakasunod ng qubit ng boxed circuit, na limitado sa mga qubit ng box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, suppose you want to figure out how to specify a Pauli Lindblad map for `\"noise1\"`. Then the order of qubits in the noise map is with respect to these qubits:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, sabihin nating gusto mong alamin kung paano tukuyin ang isang Pauli Lindblad map para sa `\"noise1\"`. Ang pagkakasunod ng mga qubit sa noise map ay batay sa mga qubit na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, if you want `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` to be noisy with `X` noise, then you should define a Pauli Lindblad map like this one because it is at index `1` of `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"
msgstr "Ibig sabihin, kung gusto mong maging noisy ang `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` na may `X` noise, dapat kang magtakda ng Pauli Lindblad map na tulad nito dahil nasa index na `1` ito ng `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same holds true for basis changes. If you want to rotate into the +1 eigenstates of the operators X, Y, and Z for qubits 0, 1, and 2 of `circuit`, respectively, then you should use the following array, recalling that the convention $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, and $Y=3$ is used in this library (and Qiskit).\n"
msgstr "Ganoon din ang totoo para sa mga basis change. Kung gusto mong i-rotate sa mga +1 eigenstate ng mga operator na X, Y, at Z para sa mga qubit 0, 1, at 2 ng `circuit`, ayon sa pagkakasunod, dapat mong gamitin ang sumusunod na array, na tandaan ang kumbensyong $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, at $Y=3$ na ginagamit sa library na ito (at sa Qiskit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the qubit ordering convention is *not* the order defined by either of the following:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang kumbensyon sa pagkakasunod ng qubit ay *hindi* ang pagkakasunod na tinutukoy ng alinman sa mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.qubits`, where `box_instruction` is a [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) whose operation is a [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), because the order of this list of qubits might depend on the order in which instructions were added to the box context, which would be a confusing convention. For example, `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` and `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` would result in different orderings.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.qubits`, kung saan ang `box_instruction` ay isang [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) na ang operasyon ay isang [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), dahil ang pagkakasunod ng listahang ito ng mga qubit ay maaaring nakadepende sa pagkakasunod ng pagdaragdag ng mga instruction sa box context, na magiging nakalilitong kumbensyon. Halimbawa, ang `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` at `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` ay magreresulta sa magkaibang pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` because these qubits might not even appear in the outer circuit. Qubits inside the actual body of `BoxOp` instructions (or any other control flow operation like `IfElseOp`) are only promised to have a consisent meaning within that scope. This would be an ill-defined convention, and hard to use in general.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` dahil maaaring hindi man lang lumitaw ang mga qubit na ito sa panlabas na circuit. Ang mga qubit sa loob ng aktwal na body ng mga `BoxOp` instruction (o anumang iba pang control flow operation tulad ng `IfElseOp`) ay ipinapangakong may pare-parehong kahulugan lamang sa loob ng scope na iyon. Magiging ill-defined ang kumbensyong ito, at mahirap gamitin sa pangkalahatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local testing with the template circuit {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"
msgstr "Lokal na pagsubok gamit ang template circuit {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") is constructed by using the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function, the output parameter values should be directly compatible with the parameters of the associated template circuit. For example, you can bind values for one of the randomizations to the template for local inspection.\n"
msgstr "Kung ang isang [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") ay binuo gamit ang function na [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\"), ang mga output parameter value ay dapat direktang compatible sa mga parameter ng kaugnay na template circuit. Halimbawa, maaari kang mag-bind ng mga value para sa isa sa mga randomization sa template para sa lokal na inspeksyon.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lets you verify that the samplex is outputing samples that are expected. For example, the following code casts the bound circuit to a [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object and composes with the bitflip Paulis to visually inspect that all three randomizations are logically equivalent to the base circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pinapayagan ka nitong i-verify na ang samplex ay naglalabas ng mga sample na inaasahan. Halimbawa, kino-cast ng sumusunod na code ang bound circuit sa isang [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object at kino-compose sa mga bitflip na Pauli para biswal na suriin na lahat ng tatlong randomization ay lohikal na katumbas ng base circuit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, the following code passes output parameter values and the template to a sampler to simulate 10,000 shots of all randomizations, and compares the resulting expectation values (only of the alpha register) to the expectation values of a base circuit simulation.\n"
msgstr "Gayundin, ipinapasa ng sumusunod na code ang mga output parameter value at ang template sa isang sampler para i-simulate ang 10,000 shot ng lahat ng randomization, at ikinukumpara ang mga nagresultang expectation value (ng alpha register lang) sa mga expectation value ng simulation ng base circuit.\n"
